{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2633 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d5bdde7e7e88ec22fa9cb0f5bba2c2e58130ea2b2ad8b92e022662b03a644a68" :edb/db-before-t 2632 :edb/db-after-t 2633 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535945 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:11:21.170Z" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147299 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\dfrac{3}{s^2 + 9}$." 13194139535945 false] [17592186147299 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\dfrac{3}{s^2 + 9}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147299 1145 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{\\sin 3t} &= \\frac{3}{s^{2} + 3^{2}} = \\frac{3}{s^{2} + 9}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{3}{s^{2} + 9}} &= L^{-1}{L{\\sin 3t}} \\\\\n&= \\sin 3t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535945 false] [17592186147299 1145 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+{3}^{2}}=\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} & ={L}^{-1}{L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147300 1100 "Compute $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\dfrac{7}{s - 9}\\right\\}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147300 1100 "Compute $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\dfrac{e^{-3s}}{7}\\right\\}$." 13194139535945 false] [17592186147300 1145 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{δ_{3}(t)} &= e^{-3s}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\delta_3(t) = \\delta(t-3)\n$$\n\nis the Dirac delta function.\n\nTherefore, using the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{e^{-3s}}{7}} &= \\frac{1}{7}L^{-1}{e^{-3s}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}L^{-1}{L{δ_{3}(t)}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}δ_{3}(t)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535945 false] [17592186147300 1145 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{9t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-9},\\,s>9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{9t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-9} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{9t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} \\\\ {e}^{9t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} & ={e}^{9t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}}=7\\cdot {e}^{9t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{7}{s-9}}=7{e}^{9t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147301 1100 "Find $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\}$ for $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}$." 13194139535945 false] [17592186147301 1100 "Find $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\}$ for $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147301 1145 "First, we decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s} =\\dfrac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{u_{1}(t)} &= \\frac{e^{-s}}{s}, s > 0, \\\\\nL{1} &= \\frac{1}{s}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nu_1(t)=u(t-1)\n$$\n\nis the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\frac{2}{s}} &= 4L^{-1}{\\frac{e^{-s}}{s}} - 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\\n&= 4u_{1}(t) - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\} = f(t)= 4 u_1(t) - 2\n$$" 13194139535945 false] [17592186147301 1145 "First, we decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s} =\\dfrac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $u_1(t)=u(t-1)$ is the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}} & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =4{u}_{1}(t)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\} = f(t)= 4 u_1(t) - 2.\n$$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147302 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}$." 13194139535945 false] [17592186147302 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147302 1145 "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)} = \\dfrac{2}{s-4} + \\dfrac{1}{s+2}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{e^{4t}} &= \\frac{1}{s - 4}, s > 4, \\\\\nL{e^{-2t}} &= \\frac{1}{s + 2}, s > - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s - 4} + \\frac{1}{s + 2}} &= 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s - 4}} + L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s + 2}} \\\\\n&= 2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s) \\right\\} = f(t)=2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}\n$$" 13194139535945 false] [17592186147302 1145 "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)} = \\dfrac{2}{s-4} + \\dfrac{1}{s+2}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4, \\\\ L{{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+2},\\,s>-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s+2}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{ F(s) \\right\\} = f(t)=2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}.\n$$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186147451 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375772 13194139535945 true] [17592186147451 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375779 13194139535945 true] [17592186147451 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375786 13194139535945 true] [17592186147451 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375849 13194139535945 true] [17592186147452 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375793 13194139535945 true] [17592186147452 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375842 13194139535945 true] [17592186147452 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375856 13194139535945 true] [17592186147452 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375863 13194139535945 true] [17592186147452 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375870 13194139535945 true] [17592186147453 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375800 13194139535945 true] [17592186147453 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375807 13194139535945 true] [17592186147453 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375814 13194139535945 true] [17592186147453 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375828 13194139535945 true] [17592186147453 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375835 13194139535945 true] [17592186147454 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375821 13194139535945 true] [17592186147454 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375877 13194139535945 true] [17592186147454 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375884 13194139535945 true] [17592186147454 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375891 13194139535945 true] [17592186148098 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535945 true] [17592186148098 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\frac{6}{s^{2} - 6s}$." 13194139535945 false] [17592186148098 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186148098 1145 "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}=\\frac{6}{s(s-6)}=\\frac{1}{s-6}-\\frac{1}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{6t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-6},\\,s>6 \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}-\\frac{1}{s}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{6t}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}$ is $f(t)={e}^{6t}-1.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186148149 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535945 true] [17592186148149 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\frac{1}{s - 5}$." 13194139535945 false] [17592186148149 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-5}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186148149 1145 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-5},\\,s>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-5} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{5t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\ {e}^{5t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} & ={e}^{5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375772 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375773 13194139535945 true] [17592186375772 1089 "q-345578" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375772 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535945 true] [17592186375772 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{3}{2s-4}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375772 1113 #uuid "0e670e88-2c44-511f-9351-40c005009907" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375772 1145 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-2}=\\frac{3}{2s-4},\\,s>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2s-4} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} & =\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375774 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375775 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375776 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375777 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375778 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1041 "selection" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375774 13194139535945 true] [17592186375773 1110 #uuid "b9466531-ff06-5bed-98cb-c8e7675ac1bb" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375774 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375774 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375774 1111 #uuid "7964c6fa-f9e1-593a-b63b-91d5cfec3927" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375775 1034 "{e}^{2t}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375775 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375775 1111 #uuid "ca542323-ab02-53eb-82d4-3468434a6f06" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375776 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-2t}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375776 1111 #uuid "949b3644-6168-519c-aabe-36e86d2cc8ec" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375777 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375777 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375777 1111 #uuid "011980ae-e017-58cb-9490-f3f022e2395c" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375778 1034 "{t}^{2}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375778 1111 #uuid "a772f12f-aa38-542e-a9ec-3d93db870aca" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375779 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375780 13194139535945 true] [17592186375779 1089 "q-345579" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375779 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535945 true] [17592186375779 1100 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4}{3s+6}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375779 1113 #uuid "22354821-afe9-5543-8948-39a498baf294" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375779 1145 "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2}=\\frac{4}{3s+6},\\,s>-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3s+6} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} & =\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375781 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375782 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375783 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375784 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375785 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1041 "selection" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375783 13194139535945 true] [17592186375780 1110 #uuid "5ac2f2ea-f1b6-598b-baf2-e4171c4f386b" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375781 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375781 1111 #uuid "21e0030d-ec59-5e7f-9eaf-735a4efb5a4c" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375782 1034 "-\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375782 1111 #uuid "2448cfbf-9b76-5c65-88e6-644249a908c3" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375783 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375783 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375783 1111 #uuid "824e3daa-d5eb-5ee4-aaa4-bde78b9aa999" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375784 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{2t}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375784 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413953594