 true] [17592186375789 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375789 1111 #uuid "31bd77c6-86c5-50a8-ba51-37e67f8723ca" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375790 1034 "4{e}^{-t}" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375790 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375790 1111 #uuid "22a07863-5e7e-584c-82c6-5ba3312aeddc" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375791 1034 "{u}_{1}(t)" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375791 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375791 1111 #uuid "b4ae337e-a629-5051-852a-8c6c65015c75" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375792 1034 "4{u}_{1}(t)" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535945 true] [17592186375792 1111 #uuid "4d50a2d2-2bb5-592c-b061-d8a1e5ab7dc4" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375793 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375794 13194139535945 true] [17592186375793 1089 "q-345588" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375793 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535945 true] [17592186375793 1100 "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}.$" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375793 1113 #uuid "590cfd05-a2b8-5e45-b8f7-64d1952b203b" 13194139535945 true] [17592186375793 1145 "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}+9}-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+9}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}+9}-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}}-5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}$ is $f(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t.$" 1319413